# Build outputs
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.obj
*.lib
*.a
*.so
*.dll
*.exe
*.pdb
*.ilk

# Compiled shader artifacts (source shaders are tracked, binaries are
# not). Plan 0008 superseded ADR-0027's checked-in shaders/minimal_renderer/
# bytecode exception -- every shader's .spv and reflection JSON is now a
# generated, configuration-independent build-tree artifact under
# build*/ (already covered by the build-output rules above), never
# checked in.
*.spv

# Dependency/package manager caches
.vcpkg/
vcpkg_installed/

# IDE / editor
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.swp

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local test/debug output
*.log
/tmp/

# Machine-local Vulkan/GPU environment provenance (Plan 0011 Section
# 3.6/3.7) -- inherently specific to the machine it was filled in on;
# would be actively wrong if committed and read on any other machine.
# See tests/image_regression/current_environment.sidecar.txt.example
# for the template and setup instructions.
tests/image_regression/current_environment.sidecar.txt

# Plan 0034 Milestone 4 (ADR-0078): Gradle/Android build output and
# machine-local configuration -- android/local.properties records this
# machine's own sdk.dir (never portable across machines, same reasoning
# as the Vulkan/GPU sidecar above); android/app/src/main/assets/ is
# packageAtlantisAssets' own generated output (android/app/build.gradle),
# copied from a prior Windows build, never authored by hand. The Gradle
# wrapper JAR itself (gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar) is deliberately
# NOT listed here -- committing it is the standard, human-directed
# exception to this repository's usual no-binaries convention, so a
# clone can run ./gradlew without a pre-installed Gradle.
android/local.properties
android/.gradle/
android/app/build/
android/app/.cxx/
android/build/
android/app/src/main/assets/

# Deliberate, narrow exception to this file's own blanket *.so rule
# above -- the Vulkan Validation Layer binary
# jniLibs/README.txt documents belongs at
# android/app/src/main/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libVkLayer_khronos_validation.so
# and, unlike every other .so in this repository, IS meant to be
# committed once a future Milestone sources it (it ships prebuilt;
# there is no source to build it from here).
!android/app/src/main/jniLibs/**/*.so

# Spec 0037 repository content policy (Plan 0037 Milestone 2): large external
# content collections (>50 MB) are fetched by a pinned, SHA256-verifying
# script (tools/content/fetch_*.ps1), never committed. Their provenance and
# licence files live in tools/content/ and ARE committed.
/content/
